batches.description:
Create exactly three test files DIRECTLY under tests/ (top level only — the runner scans only tests/*.js; no tests/unit/ subdirectories). Use `const test = require('node:test');` and `const assert = require('node:assert/strict');`. CommonJS only, no npm packages, no Python/browsers.

1) tests/csv.test.js — at least 5 cases on `require('../src/core/csv.js').parseCsv`:
 - double-quoted field containing a comma (`a,"b,c"` -> `[['a','b,c']]`);
 - escaped double quotes (`"say ""hi"""` -> `say "hi"`);
 - CRLF line endings produce the same rows as LF and do not leave `\r` in fields;
 - trailing empty lines / final newline are ignored (`'a,b\n'` -> `[['a','b']]`, `'a,b\n\n'` -> `[['a','b']]`);
 - Chinese characters preserved verbatim (e.g. `'名,值\n张三,1\n'` -> `[['名','值'],['张三','1']]`);
 - plus edge cases: `parseCsv('')` -> `[]`; interior blank line preserved as `['']`; `typeof text !== 'string'` throws `TypeError`.

2) tests/stats.test.js — at least 5 cases on `require('../src/core/stats.js').columnStats`:
 - numeric column (`['n'],['1'],['2'],['3.5']` style) -> type `'number'`, total/missing correct, min/max numeric, mean rounded to 2 decimals, `unique === null`;
 - mixed-type column falls back to `'string'` with `min === null && max === null && mean === null` and a correct `unique`;
 - all-empty column -> type `'string'`, `unique === 0`, `min/max/mean === null`, `missing === total`;
 - missing count accuracy: empty and whitespace-only values both count as missing, and a data row shorter than the header counts as missing for the absent column;
 - unique count accuracy: duplicates and empty values excluded (e.g. `['a','a','',' b ','b']` -> unique 2), and header row is NEVER counted in total;
 - plus `columnStats([])` -> `[]`.

3) tests/cli.test.js — at least 2 cases on `require('../src/cli.js').run`:
 - normal path: write a temp CSV with `fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'csvstat-'))` + `fs.writeFileSync`, stub `console.log` with a spy that appends to an array, call `run(['node','src/cli.js',tmpFile])`, assert the captured output contains `'col0'` and the expected `type=` line; assert `process.exitCode` was not set to 1.
 - error path: call `run(['node','src/cli.js', path.join(tmpDir,'missing.csv')])` with `console.error` stubbed, assert the spy was called and `process.exitCode === 1`.
 - cleanup: every test must wrap its body in `try { ... } finally { fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }); }`, restore the original `console.log`/`console.error`, and restore `process.exitCode` (set back to `0`/`undefined`) so a failing assertion cannot leak a non-zero exit code into the runner.
 - Also assert `require('../src/cli.js')` does not print anything by itself (auto-exec only when `require.main === module`).

All assertions must be deterministic and must not depend on the current working directory except through the temp paths.
